NAME
       uniq - filter adjacent matching lines

SYNOPSIS
       uniq [-cdiu] [input [output]]

DESCRIPTION
       Collapses runs of identical adjacent lines. Only adjacent lines
       are compared, so the input is usually sorted first.

OPTIONS
       -c     prefix each line with the number of occurrences
       -d     print only lines that repeat
       -i     ignore case while comparing
       -u     print only lines that occur exactly once

EXAMPLES
       sort names.txt | uniq -c

SEE ALSO
       sort(1)
